Cell[TextData[{
 "In this Section we are going to cover one of the most important \
functionalities of ",
 StyleBox["xCPS",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": the variational relations. This is, in essence, the chain rule for \
variational calculus. Indeed, if we compute the variation of a function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"f", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}]], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "383a1c8d-acf3-9e47-92c2-1594a0afeed8"],
 " we obtain:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9501146582114077`*^9, 3.9501148036618843`*^9}, {
   3.95011485672637*^9, 3.9501150853789864`*^9}, {3.9501156828299046`*^9, 
   3.9501157362206345`*^9}, {3.9514792115025673`*^9, 3.9514792184243374`*^9}, 
   3.951869246445036*^9, {3.9526073743599043`*^9, 3.9526073777395253`*^9}, {
   3.954759543425189*^9, 3.954759543920702*^9}, {3.9564098778078957`*^9, 
   3.9564098831073017`*^9}, {3.9578832021549816`*^9, 
   3.9578832047676525`*^9}, {3.9578833325459876`*^9, 3.957883334875577*^9}, {
   3.958050614937807*^9, 3.9580506273468056`*^9}, {3.9581563586956635`*^9, 
   3.9581563926556816`*^9}, 
   3.959578748252924*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ac410c30-cf94-7d4c-8bae-\
ba8f402ed5a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"df", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], "dx"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], "dy", " "}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.950558777787306*^9, 3.950558913121212*^9}, {
   3.950965093094467*^9, 3.9509651190081415`*^9}, 3.950965161268156*^9, 
   3.950965291073814*^9, 3.956409842371087*^9},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellTags->
  "eq: df=chain rule",ExpressionUUID->"746bcb1e-2ad2-9247-bad6-98598f3db59d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "we see that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "f"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->"3ccfbfdc-1429-9244-a3bf-c47da15bcf63"],
 " depends variationally on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "x"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->"3b47e4ab-350d-3943-9f6d-7096f13a0896"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "y"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->"462bdcdb-5241-c245-b0e0-fa611fef6f90"],
 ". In the case of fields is trickier since more relations are possible. For \
instance, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "RicciScalar"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "2fc34727-d51e-6845-a343-78f5817476ad"],
 " depends only on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "metric"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "ca81a179-fc22-1146-ba10-de21a8cee9bb"],
 ", however, it also depends on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Ricci"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "d10eb454-88c2-9446-831b-43ef0a1e957a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Riemann"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "c269c8b1-5384-8746-bba4-266aa59539c6"],
 " (which in turn depend on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "metric"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "1dc0c1d8-874b-8343-a164-3694e1e6d104"],
 " but notice that if, for instance, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Ricci"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "e1ebbc64-1733-644f-baf0-a412e8c75236"],
 " is zero, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "RicciScalar"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "f70fd629-9f4f-f149-9e7e-dcb849f1ed6e"],
 " is zero even if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "metric"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "1a41d857-90a8-0646-b185-c8c678fc25b8"],
 " is not zero). It is important to understand that there is a hierarchy in \
this relationship:\n\nFor instance: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
  "g", "\[RightArrow]", "Riemann", "\[RightArrow]", "Ricci", "\[RightArrow]", 
   "RicciScalar"}]], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "afc895c4-a26c-5f48-9409-9b5613ad86a8"],
 ". We also have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    RowBox[{"g", "\[RightArrow]", "Christoffel"}]], "InlineCode",
    ExpressionUUID->"4c8fef68-7eaa-db4e-ae7f-9cc2989c606e"]], "InlineCode",
    ExpressionUUID->"2c3f4f1d-64d7-694d-93d4-e3bcf1be04a4"], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"516442d6-4498-5c4c-b821-663330d5802b"],
 " and many other relations. These relations actually form a graph. These and \
other well-known relations are implemented in ",
 StyleBox["xCPS",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and the user can add more. This functionality is similar to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "ImplicitTensorDepQ"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "aba93c49-89c2-234a-a443-c00d1ead579d"],
 " but on steroids!"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9526073997327447`*^9, 3.9526074174433126`*^9}, {
  3.9547595179911547`*^9, 3.9547595227885404`*^9}, {3.956409859883301*^9, 
  3.956409930363016*^9}, {3.9581563954820137`*^9, 3.9581565861192856`*^9}, {
  3.9581569144965305`*^9, 
  3.958156915314453*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"feed3785-9ffe-a142-8629-\
4e07a4879415"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is important to notice that, although relations of any kind of tensors \
can exist, the graph relation we alluded before, only makes sense for \
1-forms. Indeed, from the equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"df", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], "dx"}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], "dy"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"316880f9-16ee-a44c-ba59-eee078b495b8"],
 " we can assure that if x and y are both constant, then f is constant. \
However, if we have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[Omega]", "xy"], 
      RowBox[{"dx", "\[Wedge]", "dy"}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[Omega]", "xz"], 
      RowBox[{"dx", "\[Wedge]", "dz"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"2dfd1143-b0ed-2f45-805f-6524d65451df"],
 ", then x constant implies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f713d416-ae49-2044-a1e5-275d5a936ef8"],
 ". However, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "71fa9d2d-5d70-9d46-bf93-5e35f0c5ab8c"],
 " might not be constant but if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"y", ",", "z"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ca8263c3-6afc-3e49-806e-a18efe99f27e"],
 " are constant, then \[Omega] is zero. The relations for higher order forms \
is much more complicated."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9501146582114077`*^9, 3.9501148036618843`*^9}, {
   3.95011485672637*^9, 3.9501150853789864`*^9}, {3.9501156828299046`*^9, 
   3.9501157362206345`*^9}, {3.9514792115025673`*^9, 3.9514792184243374`*^9}, 
   3.951869246445036*^9, {3.9565207100389423`*^9, 3.9565209203303833`*^9}, 
   3.957585684172675*^9, {3.9581631617636166`*^9, 3.958163183522072*^9}, {
   3.9597489780533504`*^9, 
   3.959748989521343*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b4477c3d-acb9-1f46-b304-\
79949a4b345b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$DefInfoQ", "=", "False"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefConstantSymbol", "[", "dimen", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"DefManifold", "[", 
  RowBox[{"M", ",", "dimen", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "a", ",", "b", ",", "c", ",", "d", ",", "e", ",", "f", ",", "h", ",", "i",
      ",", "j", ",", "k", ",", "l"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v0", "[", "a", "]"}], ",", "M"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v1", "[", "a", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", 
   RowBox[{"VertDeg", "->", "1"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v2", "[", "a", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", 
   RowBox[{"VertDeg", "->", "2"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v3", "[", "a", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", 
   RowBox[{"VertDeg", "->", "3"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"alpha3", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "]"}], ",", "M", ",", 
   RowBox[{"VertDeg", "->", "3"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", "\"\<\[Alpha]3\>\""}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f3", "[", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", 
   RowBox[{"VertDeg", "->", "3"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", "\"\<F\>\""}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"alpha0", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "]"}], ",", "M", ",", 
   RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", "\"\<\[Alpha]0\>\""}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"DefTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"alpha1", "[", 
     RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "]"}], ",", "M", ",", 
    RowBox[{"VertDeg", "->", "1"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", "\"\<\[Alpha]1\>\""}]}], "]"}], "\n"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"DefCovD", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"der", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<;\>\"", ",", "\"\<D\>\""}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Torsion", "->", "True"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$DefInfoQ", "=", "True"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$UndefInfoQ", "=", "True"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.932987560855455*^9, 3.932987577577396*^9}, {
   3.948823024995694*^9, 3.948823039830458*^9}, 3.950116252680632*^9, {
   3.9501162997312355`*^9, 3.9501163046269093`*^9}, 3.950116361865635*^9, {
